   "source": [
    "## 13. Optional: time-ordered sensitivity check\n",
    "The UCI documentation says this file is ordered by date. Here the model is trained on the **first 60%** of rows in file order and tested on the **last 20%**\n",
    "(assuming file order is time order). ROC-AUC does not depend on the base rate, so it is the fair number to compare with the random-split result above;\n",
    "PR-AUC is not comparable when the base rates differ."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d96438ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Xo, yo = X_all[FEATURES].reset_index(drop=True), y_all.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "n = len(Xo); a, b = int(0.6 * n), int(0.8 * n)\n",
    "tpipe = make_pipe(HistGradientBoostingClassifier(random_state=SEED), scale=False).fit(Xo.iloc[:a], yo.iloc[:a])\n",
    "pv_t, pt_t = proba(tpipe, Xo.iloc[a:b]), proba(tpipe, Xo.iloc[b:])\n",
    "thr_t, _ = best_threshold_fbeta(yo.iloc[a:b], pv_t)\n",
    "mt = metrics_at(yo.iloc[b:], pt_t, thr_t)\n",
    "print(pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    {\"evaluation\": \"random stratified split (main results)\", \"test ROC-AUC\": test_m[\"roc_auc\"], \"test subscription rate\": y_test.mean()},\n",
    "    {\"evaluation\": \"time-ordered (first 60% train, last 20% test)\", \"test ROC-AUC\": mt[\"roc_auc\"], \"test subscription rate\": yo.iloc[b:].mean()}]).round(3).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "print(f\"Subscription rate by block: first 60% {yo.iloc[:a].mean():.1%}, next 20% {yo.iloc[a:b].mean():.1%}, last 20% {yo.iloc[b:].mean():.1%}\")"
   ]
